Repeated blocks in Qwen-family checkpoints: pinned weights and neuron responses
Copyright 2026 Jeffrey Shorthill

This release measures weight similarity between decoder blocks of the following publicly
hosted checkpoints, read by HTTP byte range at the pinned revisions in models.lock.json:

  Qwen (Alibaba): Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B, Qwen2-57B-A14B, Qwen2.5-7B, Qwen2.5-Math-7B, Qwen2.5-14B, Qwen2.5-32B,
    Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-14B, Qwen3-30B-A3B,
    Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct, Qwen3-235B-A22B,
    Qwen3-Coder-480B-A35B-Instruct, Qwen3.5-0.8B, Qwen3.5-2B, Qwen3.5-4B, Qwen3.5-9B,
    Qwen3.5-27B, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-Base, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, Qwen3.5-122B-A10B, Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, Qwen3.6-27B,
    Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, Qwen3.8-27B, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen
  Kwaipilot: KAT-V1-40B — https://huggingface.co/Kwaipilot/KAT-V1-40B
  DeepSeek: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B — https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B
  Upstage: SOLAR-10.7B-v1.0 — https://huggingface.co/upstage/SOLAR-10.7B-v1.0

Small upstream config and safetensors-index files are preserved under provenance/metadata/
so the tensor selection can be audited; they retain their upstream copyright and licenses
(see each model card). No tensor payloads are redistributed; the scanner's local tensor
cache is excluded from version control and uploads.

SOLAR's disclosed construction, used here as the calibration for a copied-then-trained block:
  Kim et al. (2023), SOLAR 10.7B: Scaling Large Language Models with Simple yet Effective
  Depth Up-Scaling. https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.15166

The scanner derives from the author's earlier release for Qwen3.6-27B
(https://github.com/ec75hash/qwen-depth-upscaling-jpp-check, Apache-2.0), which Codex
assisted with. Claude assisted with this release's scanner extensions, report code,
figures and documentation. The research direction, the unpublished September 2026 working survey whose hypotheses this
release measures, and the interpretation are Jeffrey Shorthill's.

Version 0.2.0 adds the separately documented Qwen3-14B/32B weight comparisons and Qwen3-32B Q8 response measurements. WikiText-103 text excerpts retain their upstream license declarations and attribution; see studies/qwen3_response/corpus/NOTICE.md. Capture and reduction code was developed with Codex assistance; the retained historical weight scripts were developed with Claude assistance.

The Qwen2.5-14B/32B addition includes corrected cached-capture measurements developed with Claude assistance and same-cache byte-level recomputation and packaging developed with Codex assistance; no model weights are bundled.
